  "id": "subjective-expected-utility",
  "term": "subjective expected utility",
  "definition": "Subjective expected utility is an established idea that explains choice as based on a person’s own preferences and subjective perceptions. In this view, people choose according to what they believe will be most worthwhile or beneficial.",
